" IdeaVim for JetBrains IDEs (keymap: IntelliJ GNOME).
" Vim handles text editing; IDE actions use the IDE's own shortcuts
" (Alt-Enter, Shift-F6, Alt-F7, Ctrl-B, Ctrl-Q, Shift Shift...).

" search and scrolling
set scrolloff=8
set hlsearch
set incsearch
set ignorecase
set smartcase

" J joins lines the way the IDE does (strings, comments)
set ideajoin
" no beep
set visualbell

" Shortcut conflicts: who handles each Ctrl key (n-v = normal and visual,
" i = insert, a = all modes). Vim keeps editing and navigation; the IDE gets
" its actions where the Vim meaning is rarely used.
" ":action <ID>" runs any IDE action by name; :actionlist shows the IDs.

" Vim: core editing and navigation
" half page down (IDE: duplicate line; Vim: yyp)
sethandler <C-d> a:vim
" jump forward (IDE: implement methods; Vim: :action ImplementMethods)
sethandler <C-i> a:vim
" jump back (IDE: override methods; Vim: :action OverrideMethods)
sethandler <C-o> a:vim
" redo (IDE: replace; Vim: :%s/old/new/gc)
sethandler <C-r> a:vim
" half page up (IDE: go to super method; Vim: :action GotoSuperMethod)
sethandler <C-u> a:vim
" window commands, delete word in insert (IDE: extend selection; Vim: v plus a text object, like viw, vi( or vip)
sethandler <C-w> a:vim
" scroll up (IDE: delete line; Vim: dd)
sethandler <C-y> a:vim
" escape (IDE: go to code block start; Vim: [{)
sethandler <C-[> a:vim

" Vim in normal/visual, IDE while typing
" increment number / select all (in normal mode, Vim: ggVG)
sethandler <C-a> n-v:vim i:ide
" visual block / paste (in normal mode, Vim: "+p from the system clipboard)
sethandler <C-v> n-v:vim i:ide
" decrement number / cut (in normal or visual mode, Vim: "+d to the system clipboard)
sethandler <C-x> n-v:vim i:ide

" IDE: its action is more useful than Vim's here
" go to declaration (Vim: page up)
sethandler <C-b> a:ide
" copy (Vim: cancel; use y and Esc instead)
sethandler <C-c> a:ide
" recent files (Vim: scroll one line)
sethandler <C-e> a:ide
" find in file (Vim: page down; / is enough)
sethandler <C-f> a:ide
" go to line (Vim: file info)
sethandler <C-g> a:ide
" type hierarchy (Vim: backspace in insert)
sethandler <C-h> a:ide
" insert live template (Vim: new line)
sethandler <C-j> a:ide
" commit (Vim: digraph in insert)
sethandler <C-k> a:ide
" (Vim: redraw, useless in the IDE)
sethandler <C-l> a:ide
" go to class (Vim: next line / completion in insert)
sethandler <C-n> a:ide
" parameter info, also while typing (Vim: previous line / completion in insert)
sethandler <C-p> a:ide
" quick documentation (Vim: alternative visual block)
sethandler <C-q> a:ide
" save all (Vim: nothing)
sethandler <C-s> a:ide
" update project (Vim: tag stack back)
sethandler <C-t> a:ide
" undo (Vim: suspend, meaningless in the IDE)
sethandler <C-z> a:ide
" go to code block end (Vim: go to definition; Ctrl-B does that)
sethandler <C-]> a:ide
